  "body": "You can select edges, vertices, faces and cylinder walls and say which axis each one sets (#701) - the WCS lands on the fitted frame, undoable like any other placement.\n\n## The change\n\n**App lane** - `pick::roles.rs`: `Role` (`Origin | X | Y | Z`) and `align_roles(world, picks) -> Result<Alignment, String>`, returning the same `Alignment` `pick::align`'s 3-2-1 fit already returns, so one fit law answers both. Frame law: among the axis picks present, read in the priority order Z, X, Y - first exact, second projected perpendicular, third derived to close the right-handed frame (a third axis pick is overridden wholesale, not blended). An origin pick anchors on the feature's natural centre; without one, the origin falls on the second axis pick's anchor (an edge's start, a face's centroid, a wall's centre), projected onto the first pick's plane when that pick is a face. Refusals come back as words, in order: too few picks, a duplicated role, fewer than two axes, an unresolvable datum, an unsupportable tilt, a stale feature id. Cylinder walls fit by covariance null-space (Jacobi) plus a Kasa circle, on the wall's local facets transformed by the feature's `setup_align::view_pose` - the same law the plane fit already uses.\n\n**UI lane** - the Setups page grows a \"Set WCS from features\" row (`egui_app::wcs_pick_row.rs`) over a draft module (`wcs_pick.rs`): arming it keeps the toolbar's pick mode (faces, edges, corners and walls all feed the one draft), the role box says what the next pick sets, and each viewport pick is stamped into that role's slot - re-picking a role replaces its pick in place. One draft at a time: arming this row disarms the plane-pick and axis-pick drafts and vice versa, and the wcs draft pauses while its setup row is hidden (the #664 law). Apply is gated live by `align_roles` itself - the refusal words ride the row inline and on the disabled button, so the UI's why is the command's own words - and only answers on the ACTIVE setup's row: `SetWcs` places the active setup's WCS, so a greyed Apply on another setup's row says to make that row's setup active first. Apply queues the existing undoable `CommandKind::SetWcs`; the same command the WCS pane's anchor grid already sends. No new command kind, no world writes outside commands. Rationale in `docs/decisions/701-wcs-from-features.md`.\n\n## Pins (red before the fix, green with it)\n\n- `wcs_roles::z_face_x_edge_and_origin_corner_reproduce_the_3_2_1_frame` - a Z face, X edge and origin corner digit-for-digit reproduce `align_321`.\n- `wcs_roles::the_third_axis_role_is_derived_right_handed_never_read` - three axis picks: the third is overridden wholesale and the frame is right-handed.\n- `wcs_roles::the_origin_projects_onto_a_z_face_and_anchors_on_its_centroid` - an origin vertex pick anchors on the face's centroid, projected onto its plane.\n- `wcs_roles::a_tilted_bore_wall_fits_its_real_axis_and_centre` / `a_bore_wall_picked_as_z_stands_upright_with_a_pinned_sign` - the wall fit, both flat and tilted, sign pinned by the axis role.\n- `wcs_roles::every_degenerate_role_set_is_refused_by_name` - each refusal sentence, pinned.\n- `wcs_roles::an_edge_as_the_first_axis_reads_unit_on_a_part_tipped_off_the_table` - the first-axis edge is normalised right after reading: unit length and square axes on a tipped part, origin on the block.\n- `egui_app::wcs_pick_tests::*` - five kittest tests on the live row: arming keeps the pick mode and stops the other drafts; an incomplete set greys Apply and shows the app's own words; role picks land in the draft (never in the open operation) and Apply queues one undoable `SetWcs` that undo/redo round-trips; re-picking replaces only that role's pick; and with two setups, the row on the inactive one greys Apply, queues nothing, says to make that setup active, and once active the same frame moves that setup's own WCS while the other setup's work zero stays put.\n- `wcs_pick::tests::*` - three draft-module tests: role default and mutual disarm, replace-in-place, a paused draft takes nothing.\n\n## Tested\n\n- The pin commit alone is red: at `35f399d1` the `wcs_roles` binary does not compile (no `pick::Role`/`align_roles` on main) and the ui lib does not compile (no `crate::wcs_pick`, row unwired) - the API and surface the pins demand did not exist.\n- Green at head `d2663a3f`, merged with current `origin/main` (`f490458a`): `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test wcs_roles` - 7 passed. `cargo test -p camcraft-app --lib` - 110 passed. Full `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib` (state.rs and interact.rs touched) - 538 passed, 5 ignored. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` - clean.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- MCP parity: the agent surface still takes only an absolute origin/quaternion (`set_wcs`); filed as #937 to add a feature-pick version over the same `align_roles` law.\n- Arc/circle centre picks (#705/#692) as the Origin role, now that `feature_arc` has landed - not wired here (`PickKinds.centres: false` in the wcs mode).\n- A wall picked as an axis takes its sign from the hemisphere rule, not from the origin pick as an edge does (review round 3): deterministic, but siding it by the origin pick would match what a user expects.\n\nChangelog: the Setups page can set the WCS from feature picks - click faces, edges, corners and walls in the viewport, say what each one sets, and Apply places the work zero on the fitted frame, undo and redo included (#701)\n\nFixes #701\n",
